From: Alessandro Lopez <norelec@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 19:14:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Closing or quitting the main window puts it away

The assistant lives as long as the game. Closing the main window, or quitting
from the macOS menu, hides it on macOS, where the Dock icon or the menu bring
it back, and minimizes it elsewhere. The application menu gets a "Show
ClassicAssist" item instead of Avalonia's "About Avalonia".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LFcBNQtF3Z7vfzi99BXwUe
---
 ClassicAssist.Avalonia/App.axaml.cs | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/ClassicAssist.Avalonia/App.axaml.cs b/ClassicAssist.Avalonia/App.axaml.cs
index aaf679d..cdf6dc3 100644
--- a/ClassicAssist.Avalonia/App.axaml.cs
+++ b/ClassicAssist.Avalonia/App.axaml.cs
@@ -60,6 +60,7 @@ public class App : Application
 
                 desktop.MainWindow = mainWindow;
                 UiHost.MainWindow = mainWindow;
+                WindowKeeper.Install( desktop, mainWindow );
 
                 // Shown explicitly: the lifetime only auto-shows a MainWindow that was already set
                 // when OnFrameworkInitializationCompleted returned, which by now it has.
